<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    The bundle ships the two keys its boolean transformer reads, in its OWN domain.

    ⚠️ The domain is `dataflow`, never `messages`. A bundle that hard-codes `messages` forces each
    of its consumers to break the rule this ecosystem enforces — translations split by functional
    domain, `messages` never a dumping ground. `datatable-bundle` had to gain a configurable domain
    after the fact, and 165 lines of catalogue moved with it.

    ⚠️ XLIFF rather than YAML, and English rather than French: a published package's default
    catalogue is the one a consumer overrides, so it has to be the neutral one. A French consumer
    ships `dataflow.fr.yaml` in its own `translations/` and Symfony merges it over this.
-->
